[2026-03-22T12:32:10Z] POST-TOOL-USE: INPUT: {"session_id":"56178414-c11f-4e65-b276-15b4da9222d2","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\jackw\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-jackw-Desktop-SwjshAlgoKnife\\56178414-c11f-4e65-b276-15b4da9222d2.jsonl","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jackw\\Desktop\\SwjshAlgoKnife","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"python scripts/jira_client.py comment BACK-16 \"## User Story\n\nAs a trader using SwjshAK paper trading,\nI want a unified performance dashboard showing cumulative P&L, win rates, and drawdown metrics by agent,\nSo that I can evaluate which agents and strategies are profitable before deploying real capital.\n\n## Background\n\nThe paper trading engine (src/lib/engine/paper-trading.ts) already tracks closed trades with P&L, and calculates basic performance metrics (winRate, totalPnL, maxDrawdown, sharpeRatio). The agents API (src/app/api/agents/route.ts) aggregates trade data per agent. This feature creates a visual dashboard consuming that data.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Given closed trades exist, when I open the performance dashboard, then I see cumulative P&L chart over time (line chart)\n- [ ] Given multiple agents have trades, when I view the dashboard, then I can filter/toggle by agent\n- [ ] Given agent trades exist, when I view the dashboard, then I see win rate percentage per agent\n- [ ] Given agent trades exist, when I view the dashboard, then I see R:R ratio per agent\n- [ ] Given a drawdown period occurred, when I view the dashboard, then I see max drawdown from peak displayed\n- [ ] Given multiple sessions occurred, when I view the dashboard, then I see trades-per-session breakdown\n- [ ] Given the dashboard is open, when new trades close, then metrics update without page refresh (SSE or polling)\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Live trading metrics (paper only for now)\n- P&L attribution by individual trade (just aggregates)\n- Monte Carlo simulations or forward projections\n- Sharpe ratio calculation (future enhancement - placeholder exists in engine)\n\n## Technical Notes\n\nExisting assets to leverage:\n- PaperTradingEngine.getPerformanceMetrics() - returns totalTrades, winRate, totalPnL, maxDrawdown\n- /api/agents GET - returns per-agent performance.win_rate, performance.total_pnl, performance.trades\n- lightweight-charts library already in use for TradingChart component\n- UI components available: GlowHoverCard, SplitBorderPanel (P&L-driven border), CounterAnimation\n\nSuggested approach:\n1. Create /app/dashboard/performance/page.tsx with server component\n2. Create PerformanceChart component using lightweight-charts\n3. Create AgentMetricCard component using SplitBorderPanel\n4. Add API endpoint /api/performance/aggregate for dashboard data\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- Paper trading engine must have trades to display (can seed test data)\n- Agents API must return performance data (already implemented)\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Should we persist historical snapshots for equity curve replay, or calculate from trades on-demand?\n- Should strategy clustering use k-means or manual tagging?\n\n---\nPriority: P1 (High)\nEstimate: 16-24 hours (pending Hunter review)\nLabels: feature, ui, dashboard, paper-trading\nRequested By: Product backlog curation\" 2>&1","description":"Add groomed user story and acceptance criteria to BACK-16"},"tool_response":{"stdout":"Added comment to BACK-16\r","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UgoQSnTDW3opzpW8cyWbuf"}
