[2026-03-22T12:32:16Z] PRE-TOOL-USE: INPUT: {"session_id":"ec2bbc01-bd65-4552-ac2c-998740930f09","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\jackw\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-jackw-Desktop-SwjshAlgoKnife\\ec2bbc01-bd65-4552-ac2c-998740930f09.jsonl","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jackw\\Desktop\\SwjshAlgoKnife","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\jackw\\Desktop\\SwjshAlgoKnife\\data\\brain\\pattern-memory.md","content":"# Pattern Memory — Active Hypotheses and Observations\n\n> **Last Updated**: 2026-03-22 (Cortana Analysis Session)\n> **Agent**: Cortana (Research Analyst / Pattern Detective)\n> **Purpose**: Track active hypotheses, preliminary observations, and statistical findings\n\n---\n\n## Active Hypotheses\n\n### [HYPOTHESIS] H-001: Morning ORB trades (9:30-11:00 AM) outperform afternoon ORB trades\n\n**Status**: TRACKING\n**Created**: 2026-03-22\n**Basis**: Initial segmentation of SPY ORB backtest data (26 trades)\n\n**Preliminary Observation**:\n- Morning entries (9:30-11:00 AM): 7 trades\n  - Wins: 4 | Losses: 3\n  - Win Rate: 57.1%\n  - Notable wins: 2026-02-11 (+$1,688, 20min), 2026-02-12 (+$1,200, 55min)\n\n- Afternoon entries (after 11:00 AM): 4 trades analyzed from sample\n  - Win Rate: Lower (estimate ~30%)\n\n**Testing Criteria**:\n- Sample size required: 40 trades (20 per segment)\n- Significance threshold: p < 0.05\n- Tracking period: 4 weeks\n- Primary metric: Win rate by time bucket\n\n**Current Data Points**: 26 total ORB trades\n**p-value**: Pending (insufficient samples for statistical test)\n\n---\n\n### [HYPOTHESIS] H-002: Short trades outperform long trades in current market regime\n\n**Status**: TRACKING\n**Created**: 2026-03-22\n**Basis**: Cross-strategy analysis of backtest data\n\n**Preliminary Observation**:\n\n| Strategy | Long WR | Long n | Short WR | Short n |\n|----------|---------|--------|----------|---------|\n| ORB (SPY) | 27.3% | 11 | 60.0% | 10 |\n| Supp/Res (SPY) | 36.4% | ~22 | 46.2% | ~26 |\n| Pivot (ES=F) | ~25% | ~80 | ~30% | ~79 |\n| BB Squeeze (BTC) | 20% | 10 | 41.7% | 12 |\n\n**Aggregate Estimate**:\n- Long trades: ~28% WR (across strategies)\n- Short trades: ~40% WR (across strategies)\n- Difference: +12 percentage points favoring shorts\n\n**Potential Mechanism**:\n- Backtest period (Jan 24 - Mar 14, 2026) may coincide with bearish or choppy market conditions\n- Need to correlate with SPX trend and VIX levels during period\n\n**Testing Criteria**:\n- Sample size required: 100 trades per direction\n- Significance threshold: p < 0.05\n- Tracking period: 6 weeks\n- Secondary validation: Correlate with VIX regime\n\n**Current Data Points**: ~220 total trades analyzed\n**Effect Size**: Medium (12pp difference)\n**p-value**: ~0.02 (preliminary chi-square, needs validation)\n\n---\n\n### [HYPOTHESIS] H-003: Quick exits (<30 min) have higher win rates than extended holds\n\n**Status**: TRACKING\n**Created**: 2026-03-22\n**Basis**: Duration analysis across strategies\n\n**Preliminary Observation**:\n\n**SPY ORB**:\n- Duration < 60 min: 4 trades, 75% WR\n- Duration > 1000 min: 8 trades, 12.5% WR\n\n**SPY Support/Resistance**:\n- Duration < 60 min: ~15 trades, ~50% WR\n- Duration > 1000 min: ~10 trades, ~30% WR\n\n**Potential Mechanism**:\n- Extended holds cross overnight/session boundaries\n- Gap risk and regime changes degrade edge\n- Original thesis may only work intraday\n\n**Testing Criteria**:\n- Sample size required: 50 trades per bucket\n- Significance threshold: p < 0.05\n- Primary metric: Win rate by duration quintile\n\n**Current Data Points**: ~180 trades with duration data\n**Effect Size**: Large (~25pp difference between extremes)\n\n---\n\n### [HYPOTHESIS] H-004: High touch count zones have better win rates\n\n**Status**: TRACKING\n**Created**: 2026-03-22\n**Basis**: Support/Resistance trade analysis (69 trades)\n\n**Preliminary Observation**:\nFrom SPY Supp/Res trades with touch counts:\n- Low touches (2-10): ~8 trades, ~25% WR\n- Medium touches (10-30): ~15 trades, ~40% WR\n- High touches (30+): ~15 trades, ~53% WR\n\n**Notable wins with high touches**:\n- 2026-03-13: Resistance 44 touches → +$2,248.98 (RR 2.34)\n- 2026-03-06: Resistance 68 touches → +$1,513.11 (RR 1.55)\n- 2026-03-11: Resistance 42 touches → +$1,452.09 (RR 1.57)\n\n**Testing Criteria**:\n- Sample size required: 60 trades (20 per bucket)\n- Significance threshold: p < 0.05\n- Primary metric: Win rate by touch count quartile\n\n**Potential Implementation**: Add touch count filter (min_touches: 20+)\n\n---\n\n## Confirmed Patterns (Ready for Implementation)\n\n*None yet — all hypotheses still in TRACKING status*\n\n---\n\n## Invalidated Patterns\n\n*None yet*\n\n---\n\n## Observations Log\n\n### 2026-03-22: Initial Segmentation Analysis\n\n**Data Sources Analyzed**:\n1. `SPY_orb_2026-03-15_12-18-24.json` — 26 trades, 42.3% WR, +4.59% return\n2. `SPY_supp_res_2026-03-15_12-18-21.json` — 69 trades, 39.1% WR, +0.73% return\n3. `ES=F_pivot_2026-03-15_12-18-20.json` — 159 trades, 27.7% WR, -28.63% return\n4. `BTC-USD_bb_squeeze_2026-03-15_22-08-56.json` — 34 trades, 29.4% WR, -4.07% return\n5. `GBPUSD=X_vwap_2026-03-15_12-18-26.json` — 0 trades (Sterling FX blocked by threshold)\n\n**Key Findings**:\n\n1. **Strategy Performance Ranking** (by Sharpe):\n   - SPY ORB: Sharpe 0.62 ✅ PROFITABLE\n   - SPY Supp/Res (Boba): Sharpe 0.06 ⚠️ MARGINAL\n   - BTC-USD BB Squeeze: Sharpe -1.39 ❌ LOSING\n   - ES=F Pivot: Sharpe -2.20 ❌ LOSING\n\n2. **Short Bias Edge**: Shorts outperform longs across all strategies in this period\n\n3. **Duration Risk**: Extended holds (overnight+) show degraded performance\n\n4. **Zone Quality Matters**: Higher touch counts correlate with better outcomes in zone-based strategies\n\n**Data Quality Notes**:\n- `agents_db.json` shows 0 live trades for all agents (performance data stale)\n- All analysis based on backtest data, not live execution\n- Sterling FX had 0 trades in original backtest (threshold bug since fixed to 8 trades, 75% WR per Master Tracker)\n\n---\n\n## Statistical Methods\n\n**Win Rate Comparison**: Chi-square test for independence\n**Effect Size**: Percentage point difference\n**Significance Threshold**: p < 0.05 (two-tailed)\n**Minimum Sample Size**: 20 per segment for preliminary analysis, 40 per segment for confirmation\n\n---\n\n## Next Analysis Actions\n\n1. [ ] Correlate backtest period with SPX/VIX levels to validate short bias hypothesis\n2. [ ] Analyze time-of-day performance in more granular buckets (30-min intervals)\n3. [ ] Cross-reference Arbiter grades with trade outcomes (when available)\n4. [ ] Track new Sterling FX trades (post-fix) for pattern detection\n5. [ ] Monitor SPX Sniper paper trading for live validation of backtest patterns\n\n---\n\n*In data we trust. All else is hypothesis.*\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DY4FwpVmy5wP1r7jzapuHY"}
