[2026-03-22T12:32:49Z] POST-TOOL-USE: INPUT: {"session_id":"56178414-c11f-4e65-b276-15b4da9222d2","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\jackw\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-jackw-Desktop-SwjshAlgoKnife\\56178414-c11f-4e65-b276-15b4da9222d2.jsonl","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jackw\\Desktop\\SwjshAlgoKnife","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"python scripts/jira_client.py comment BACK-13 \"## User Story\n\nAs a trader developing strategies for SwjshAK,\nI want an automated research loop that mutates strategy parameters, backtests variations, and scores them against profit/Sharpe/drawdown metrics,\nSo that I can discover optimal parameter combinations without manual trial-and-error.\n\n## Background\n\nBACK-11 (Done) completed the AutoResearch loop architecture with prepare.py + strategy.py. This ticket builds the full implementation: a self-improving system that:\n1. Fetches OHLCV data\n2. Mutates strategy parameters within defined bounds\n3. Backtests mutations using the existing engine\n4. Scores results (profit factor, Sharpe ratio, max drawdown)\n5. Keeps improvements via genetic/evolutionary selection\n\nExisting foundation:\n- MarketSimulator (src/lib/engine/simulator.ts) generates synthetic data\n- PaperTradingEngine provides trade execution and metrics\n- Strategy classes have configurable parameters (e.g., ORB has window sizes)\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Given a strategy class with tunable parameters, when I run the optimizer, then it generates N parameter mutations\n- [ ] Given mutations exist, when backtested, then each mutation produces scored results (profit, Sharpe, maxDD)\n- [ ] Given scored results, when selection runs, then top performers are kept and mutated further\n- [ ] Given an optimization run completes, when I view results, then I see the best parameter set discovered\n- [ ] Given the optimizer is running, when I check status, then I see current generation and best score\n- [ ] Given a parameter has bounds (min, max), when mutations generate, then values stay within bounds\n- [ ] Given the optimizer finds an improvement, when it completes, then the result is persisted to disk\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- GPU-accelerated backtesting\n- Multi-objective optimization (Pareto frontier)\n- Real-time parameter adaptation during live trading\n- Integration with external ML frameworks (keep it simple)\n\n## Technical Notes\n\nSuggested architecture:\n1. Create src/lib/autoresearch/Optimizer.ts - main loop\n2. Create src/lib/autoresearch/Mutation.ts - parameter variation logic\n3. Create src/lib/autoresearch/Scorer.ts - fitness function\n4. Create src/lib/autoresearch/Backtester.ts - run strategy over historical data\n5. Create scripts/run_autoresearch.ts - CLI entrypoint\n\nKey decisions needed:\n- Mutation strategy: random walk, genetic crossover, or Bayesian optimization?\n- Population size and generation count defaults\n- Historical data source: Yahoo Finance (existing) or synthetic?\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- BaseStrategy classes must expose parameter metadata (current: hardcoded values)\n- Historical data fetcher (YahooFinance.ts exists)\n- PaperTradingEngine for trade simulation\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Should we use a genetic algorithm (crossover + mutation) or simpler hill climbing?\n- What's the minimum backtest period for statistical significance? (30 trades? 100 trades?)\n- Should results auto-update strategy defaults, or require manual approval?\n\n---\nPriority: P2 (needs research phase first)\nEstimate: 30-40 hours (complex - multi-phase)\nLabels: research, ml, automation, feature\nRequested By: Product backlog curation\n\nNOTE: This is a large initiative. Recommend breaking into subtasks:\n1. BACK-13a: Parameter metadata extraction from strategies\n2. BACK-13b: Backtester implementation with historical data\n3. BACK-13c: Mutation/scoring logic\n4. BACK-13d: Optimization loop and persistence\n5. BACK-13e: CLI and reporting UI\" 2>&1","description":"Add groomed user story and acceptance criteria to BACK-13"},"tool_response":{"stdout":"Added comment to BACK-13\r","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"tool_use_id":"toolu_019gi574zAJodnEZKYnAZ5Rh"}
