[2026-03-22T12:33:18Z] POST-TOOL-USE: INPUT: {"session_id":"56178414-c11f-4e65-b276-15b4da9222d2","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\jackw\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-jackw-Desktop-SwjshAlgoKnife\\56178414-c11f-4e65-b276-15b4da9222d2.jsonl","cwd":"C:\\Users\\jackw\\Desktop\\SwjshAlgoKnife","permission_mode":"default","hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Bash","tool_input":{"command":"python scripts/jira_client.py comment BACK-15 \"## User Story\n\nAs a trader using SwjshAK strategies,\nI want signals to be evaluated across multiple timeframes (5m/15m/1h/4h/daily) with confluence scoring,\nSo that I only take trades when the higher timeframes confirm the lower timeframe signal, improving win rate.\n\n## Background\n\nThe Three Ducks strategy (src/lib/engine/strategies/threeDucks.ts) already proxies multi-timeframe analysis using different SMA windows on a single timeframe feed. This ticket formalizes a proper MTF Confluence Engine that:\n1. Maintains separate indicator state per timeframe\n2. Scores signal quality based on alignment (0-100 confluence score)\n3. Escalates position sizing based on confluence level\n4. Can be used as a filter layer by any strategy\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Given a signal on 5m timeframe, when confluence engine runs, then it checks 15m, 1h, 4h, daily for alignment\n- [ ] Given alignment across 3+ timeframes, when scored, then confluence score >= 60%\n- [ ] Given full alignment (all 5 timeframes), when scored, then confluence score = 100%\n- [ ] Given confluence score >= 80%, when position sizing runs, then size is increased (e.g., 1.5x base)\n- [ ] Given confluence score < 40%, when signal evaluated, then signal is suppressed (not executed)\n- [ ] Given the engine is active, when market data arrives, then each timeframe's indicators update independently\n- [ ] Given a strategy integrates with confluence engine, when it generates signal, then score is attached to signal metadata\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Timeframe-specific strategy configurations (same strategy params across TFs)\n- Real-time timeframe aggregation (assumes data pre-aggregated)\n- Custom weighting per timeframe (equal weighting for v1)\n\n## Technical Notes\n\nExisting related code:\n- ThreeDucksStrategy uses 3 SMA windows as TF proxy (60, 240, 1440)\n- BaseStrategy has intelContext for regime detection\n- Signal type has notes field for metadata\n\nSuggested architecture:\n1. Create src/lib/engine/confluence/MTFEngine.ts - timeframe state management\n2. Create src/lib/engine/confluence/ConfluenceScorer.ts - alignment scoring\n3. Create src/lib/engine/confluence/TimeframeAggregator.ts - candle aggregation\n4. Modify Signal type to include confluenceScore field\n5. Modify RiskEngine to factor confluence into position sizing\n\nTimeframe data structure:\n- 5m: Primary signal timeframe\n- 15m: Immediate trend confirmation\n- 1h: Intraday bias\n- 4h: Swing bias\n- Daily: Major trend direction\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- YahooFinance.ts can fetch different intervals (needs verification)\n- BaseStrategy must expose a method to evaluate without executing\n- RiskEngine must accept confluence multiplier\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- Should we support custom timeframe sets per market (e.g., crypto 24/7 vs forex sessions)?\n- What indicator(s) determine alignment? (EMA position, trend direction, RSI zone?)\n- Should confluence decay over time if signal not taken?\n\n---\nPriority: P2 (Medium)\nEstimate: 20-28 hours\nLabels: research, signals, feature\nRequested By: Product backlog curation\" 2>&1","description":"Add groomed user story and acceptance criteria to BACK-15"},"tool_response":{"stdout":"Added comment to BACK-15\r","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C9NrUYecuj3FMy4ZUtLKBb"}
